  "title": "Static routes between two sites",
  "estimatedMinutes": 15,
  "instructions": "## Two routers, no routes\n\nThe main campus (`192.168.1.0/24`, router R1) and the annex (`192.168.2.0/24`, router R2) are joined by the link `10.0.0.0/30`. Every interface and gateway is correct, but the routers only know their **directly connected** networks.\n\n## Do this\n\n1. Ping the annex server from PC1 and read where the packet stops.\n2. Click **R1** and add a static route to `192.168.2.0/24` via R2's link address.\n3. Ping again. Notice the request now arrives but the **reply** cannot get back: R2 has no route to the campus.\n4. Click **R2** and add the return route (a default route `0.0.0.0/0` via R1 is fine here).\n5. Press **Check my network**.",
